        "Content": "Luxurious 4 Bedroom Semi-Detached House -174 m²"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "11 Cois Cuain is a most delightful attractive property, recently refreshed presented to the market in walk-in condition.\r\nDrop your bags and head straight out to the beach !\r\nBuilt in 2006, this steel framed property is part of a mid-density development, containing 37 units.\r\nCois Cuain is the first development on your right as you enter one of West Cork's best loved and un-spoilt villages, Courtmacsherry.\r\nThe property has an East to West orientation, sun filled, sun drenched, during the Summer months, bright and cheerful all year round.\r\nAccommodation consists of a very welcoming Entrance Hall, Large Kitchen/Dining, restful Living Room, Utility Room, WC, splendid Conservatory on the ground floor.\r\nThe first floor has 4 beautiful Bedrooms (1 ensuite ) Main Bathroom, and a fully floored, insulated attic 30 q. mts. ( 2 large velux windows installed )\r\nWe have been advised that there is adequate head height to construct a permanent stairs to the attic, therefore making it a 5 Bedroom residence,\r\nThere's more!\r\nIf you can drag yourself away from the splendid light filled Conservatory, step outside to a lovingly tended, flower filled colourful garden\r\nThe owner has spent many long hours out here from dawn to dusk, happily beavering away and is very very proud of her finished product, the new owner just has to maintain what is already there, more time for relaxing and enjoyment.\r\nThe property comes with a B 3 Energy Rating., and will qualify for a Green Energy Mortgage Rate.\r\nParking space for 3 + cars, large communal play area to the front, safe for kids\r\nThe property is absolutely stunning, one of the best presented in the Estate. you would be proud to have it as a permanent home, or would be considered very lucky to have it as a Summer Residence.\r\nIts a lot to take in, but every word is true\r\nIf you don't believe me, go to the Nationwide Programme on RTE Player on Courtmacsherry, presented over the last few weeks and you will be very impressed by the presentation and more so by the very proud contribution made by the very welcoming Courtmacsherry residents.\r\nServices: Main Sewage, Main Water, OFCH, Stove.\r\n\r\nCourtmacsherry is a tidal harbour, and its broad expansive waters lend itself to a variety of safe and sheltered sailing and leisure activities.\r\nThis charming village was formerly the home of the Earl of Shannon who planted many exotic trees, shrubs, and woods around the village\r\nThe village of Courtmacsherry grew in Victorian times as a haven for holidaymakers from the city of Cork.\r\nThe village consists of a single long street on the South shore of Courtmacsherry Bay, with thick woods on rising ground behind.\r\nThe woods continue beyond the village Eastwards to the open sea, ending abruptly at Wood Point.\r\nBetween the village and \"The Point \" the trees run right to the waters edge and there are several natural bathing coves along the way.\r\nProudly, the village is the home of the fastest of the RNLI fleet of all-weather lifeboats.\r\nToday, Courtmacsherry has a vibrant community with several developments taking place, from improved facilities such as the refurbished pier and pontoon for boats and yachts to the promenade and tennis court, and the much used shoreline walkway from Timoleague to Courtmacsherry\r\nThe Village has many fine pubs and restaurants with local entertainment nightly."
      },
